C2C.FUSER(5)                      C2C Manual                     C2C.FUSER(5)

NAME
    c2c.fuser — the cache fuser: the only trainable part

DESCRIPTION
    The fuser implements the fused-cache update of the paper, Eq. (3):

        C_f[n] = C_n(X) + F_n( C_n(X), C^S_{G(n)}(X) )

    and the decoding Eq. (4):

        y_{i+1} = P( y_i | C_f(X) + C(Y_[0:i]) )

    One fuser clone exists per mapped layer pair (nn.Module clones, nn.
    Sequential, nn.ModuleList). Its pipeline, following Fig. 5:

      cache -> concat -> [pre-projection] -> projection
            -> dynamic weighting -> feature fusion -> x gate -> + -> fused

    Modules:

    Projection
        Concatenation of the Receiver and the Sharer cache features
        along the feature axis, a projection layer and a feature-fusion
        layer, activation in between (gelu by default).

    DynamicWeighting
        Input-aware head modulation: statistics per attention head
        (mean and max over the token axis) are pooled, passed through a
        small modulation network, and the projected information is
        reweighted per token/query, one weight per head. Beware the two
        heads (see c2c.config(5), section HEADS).

    Gate
        A learnable per-layer scalar, soft-sampled with the
        Gumbel-Sigmoid trick and annealed linearly, 1.0 -> 0.001 across
        the training steps (FR-07); differentiable during training, hard
        binary at inference. The gate makes the fusion selective and the
        selection learnable.

    RESIDUAL (FR-03): the fusion never destructively overwrites the
    Receiver's cache. The ablation ordering of Table 8 - pure
    projection 20.70, +Fuse 44.88, +Gate 47.95 - must be reproducible;
    a build that cannot reproduce the ordering fails review.

    C2C-C (App. A.1.3): the optional 3-layer-MLP pre-projection of the
    Sharer cache into the Receiver's dimensionality before the
    concatenation, selected via configuration, not a second binary.

    BLEND (FR-08): a configurable fraction of the cache may be replaced
    by fused entries; traversal former (front-to-back) or latter
    (back-to-front). Above 50 % the accuracy must rise monotonically
    (App. A.2.4, Fig. 11).

SEE ALSO
    c2c(1), c2c.config(5), c2c.engines(7), the paper, the tests.

